Package: slurmpilot
Title: Auto-Profiling SLURM HPC Orchestration and Async Shiny Offloading
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Marcus",
        family = "Harris",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
        email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"
    )
Description: Eliminates manual 'SLURM' scripting, blind memory and walltime
    guessing, and 'Shiny' server freezes for compute-heavy R workflows. Runs
    empirical micro-pilot replications in isolated child processes to measure
    true peak resident memory and runtime distributions, computes optimal
    'SLURM' array chunking and resource flags, scans project environments to
    emit reproducible 'Apptainer' container recipes and batch scripts,
    orchestrates remote 'SSH'/'SLURM' or local parallel mock-'SLURM' execution
    with atomic chunk checkpointing and surgical retries, and provides
    non-blocking 'bslib'/'Shiny' telemetry modules.
